  "reason": "The strongest result so far is config_002, where multiprofile RNA with PCA and avgpool reaches 0.591 accuracy, clearly above single-profile RNA (0.485) and far above image-only ResNet50 (0.208). This suggests multiprofile RNA is promising, but it is still unclear whether transformer aggregation can improve over avgpool. config_003 changes only the aggregation method from avgpool to transformer while keeping the same RNA encoder and multiprofile setting, so it directly isolates the effect of aggregation. This is the best next experiment because it exploits the most promising direction, reduces uncertainty about a key design choice, and establishes a stronger RNA-only baseline before testing more complex multimodal fusion."
